---
description: Grounding & door-package coupling — worked example
alwaysApply: true
---

A real RFQ (a hydraulic freight elevator modernization) was wrongly qualified with 7 matched_items. On inspection: two entries were the same infra-red door detector counted twice; a "nudging" door by-pass clause was really a control-logic requirement; "roller guide assemblies" was wrong because the schedule actually specified "sliding guides"; and "elevator governors" plus "unidirectional car safeties" appeared nowhere in the spec for this unit at all. The door operator schedule row read "new harmonic," a brand not on FTL's supported OEM list. Once de-duplicated and grounded, the ONLY real match was the single infra-red door detector — and per the door-package coupling rule, FTL's call was to disqualify rather than quote that detector alone. If other items like governors or safeties were present, it would have qualified.
